# =============================================================================
# Line-ending normalisation
# =============================================================================
# CityGuide is developed on Windows but built and deployed on Linux (Render,
# Vercel, Supabase). Without this file, Git's default `core.autocrlf` behaviour
# can commit CRLF line endings, which breaks shell scripts and can subtly change
# SQL and JSON parsing on the Linux side.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect text files and store them with LF in the
# repository, checking them out with the platform-native ending locally.
# =============================================================================

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF to run under cmd.exe.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text

# Database files are binary even though the extension looks harmless.
*.db binary
*.db-wal binary
*.db-shm binary

# Keep the lockfile byte-for-byte stable; CI installs depend on it.
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf -diff
